  "final_answer": "The script works correctly. Output for `input.csv`:\n\n```json\n[{\"item\": \"rice\", \"quantity\": 4}, {\"item\": \"soap\", \"quantity\": 3}]\n```\n\nDetails:\n- `\" Soap \"` and `\"SOAP\"` normalize to `\"soap\"` and merge (2 + 1 = 3)\n- `\"Rice\"` \u2192 `\"rice\"`, quantity 4\n- Sorted by normalized item name, emitted as a JSON array of `{\"item\": ..., \"quantity\": ...}` objects\n- Exit 0, no stderr.",
  "script": "import csv\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\ndef main():\n    path = sys.argv[1]\n    with open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as fh:\n        rows = csv.DictReader(fh)\n        acc = defaultdict(int)\n        for r in rows:\n            name = \" \".join(r[\"item\"].split()).casefold()\n            if not name:\n                continue\n            q = r[\"quantity\"].strip()\n            acc[name] += int(q) if q else 1\n    out = [{\"item\": k, \"quantity\": v} for k, v in acc.items()]\n    out.sort(key=lambda e: e[\"item\"])\n    json.dump(out, sys.stdout, ensure_ascii=False)\n    sys.stdout.write(\"\\n\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()",
